![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

To adhere to the general rules regarding loading parsed files and validating collections of data, we should explicitly validate the parsed file shape, check for and record malformed entries as structured validation failures, and skip further processing of those entries to avoid runtime property access errors. Additionally, this ensures that if a critical identifier like `question_key` or `storage_key` is missing, we fail closed rather than constructing a malformed key.

```javascript
function selectTextFirstRows(sourceRows, sourceMapPath, diagnostics = []) {
  const validRows = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < sourceRows.length; i++) {
    const row = sourceRows[i];
    if (!row || typeof row !== 'object') {
      diagnostics.push({
        code: 'malformed_entry',
        index: i,
        reason: 'Row is null or not an object',
        severity: 'high',
      });
      continue;
    }
    if (!row.question_key || !row.storage_key) {
      diagnostics.push({
        code: 'malformed_entry',
        index: i,
        reason: 'Row is missing required identifier fields (question_key: ' + row.question_key + ', storage_key: ' + row.storage_key + ')',
        severity: 'high',
      });
      continue;
    }
    if (row.requires_image_context === false) {
      validRows.push(row);
    }
  }

  return validRows.map((row) => ({
    question_key: row.question_key,
    question_row_id: row.question_row_id,
    storage_key: row.storage_key,
    subject_code: row.subject_code,
    paper_code: row.paper_code,
    question_ref: row.question_ref,
    year: row.year,
    session: row.session,
    paper_number: row.paper_number,
    variant: row.variant,
    q_number: row.q_number,
    source_pdf: row.source_pdf,
    primary_topic_path: row.primary_topic_path,
    normalized_text_present: row.normalized_text_present,
    normalized_plain_text_status: row.normalized_plain_text_status,
    text_only_addressable: row.text_only_addressable === true,
    requires_image_context: false,
    has_diagram: row.has_diagram === true,
    table_heavy: row.table_heavy === true,
    source_visual_requirement: row.source_visual_requirement,
    question_availability: row.question_availability,
    display_posture: row.display_posture,
    figure_asset_posture: row.figure_asset_posture,
    rights_display_status: row.rights_display_status,
    evidence_availability_status: row.evidence_availability_status,
    method_diagnostic_posture: row.method_diagnostic_posture,
    method_confidence_blocks_availability: row.method_confidence_blocks_availability === true,
    student_display_eligible_final: row.student_display_eligible_final === true,
    source_refs: {
      source_map_row: sourceRowRef(sourceMapPath, row.question_key),
      ...row.source_refs,
    },
    blockers: asArray(row.blockers),
    runtime_logging_key: row.question_key + '::text_first_runtime_wording',
    lineage: {
      generated_by: 'build-text-first-runtime-wording-handoff.mjs',
      generated_at: DEFAULT_GENERATED_AT,
      source_generated_by: row.lineage?.generated_by ?? null,
      source_generated_at: row.lineage?.generated_at ?? null,
    },
  }));
}
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When validating collections of data, explicitly check for and record malformed entries as structured validation failures, and skip further processing of those entries to avoid runtime property access errors.
2. When reading input collections, validate that key fields are non-empty and exist in the supported registry, skip invalid entries, and return structured diagnostics that flow into the package validator.
</details>

