![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

Validate the parsed file shape of `sourceMap` and `sourceValidator` when loading them, and pass the `diagnostics` array to `selectTextFirstRows` to ensure malformed entries are properly recorded.

```javascript
function buildHandoff({ sourceMap, sourceValidator, root, paths, generatedAt, diagnostics }) {
  if (!sourceMap || typeof sourceMap !== 'object') {
    diagnostics.push({
      code: 'malformed_input_file',
      role: 'full_beta_runtime_source_map',
      path: paths.sourceMapIn,
      reason: 'Source map is null or not an object',
      severity: 'critical',
    });
  } else if (!Array.isArray(sourceMap.rows)) {
    diagnostics.push({
      code: 'malformed_input_file',
      role: 'full_beta_runtime_source_map',
      path: paths.sourceMapIn,
      reason: 'Source map rows is not an array',
      severity: 'critical',
    });
  }

  if (!sourceValidator || typeof sourceValidator !== 'object') {
    diagnostics.push({
      code: 'malformed_input_file',
      role: 'full_beta_runtime_source_map_validator_result',
      path: paths.sourceMapValidatorIn,
      reason: 'Source validator result is null or not an object',
      severity: 'critical',
    });
  }

  const sourceRows = asArray(sourceMap?.rows);
  const rows = selectTextFirstRows(sourceRows, paths.sourceMapIn, diagnostics).map((row) => ({
    ...row,
    lineage: {
      ...row.lineage,
      generated_at: generatedAt,
    },
  }));
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When loading parsed files (such as JSON), validate the parsed file shape, record malformed entry diagnostics, skip bad entries, and pass those diagnostics into the package validator to ensure it fails closed.
</details>

